# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore -- Covio Device Manager (root, project-wide)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RE-1 (Release Engineering, Repository Hygiene & Governance Foundation).
# This is the project-wide catch-all. tools/device-manager/.gitignore already
# exists and covers that package's own specifics (node_modules/, dist/,
# *.log) -- the patterns here are broader/defensive so the SAME kind of
# generated artifact is never accidentally trackable from anywhere else in
# the tree, not just that one directory.
# ==============================================================================

# ---- Firmware build outputs (PlatformIO) ------------------------------------
# Modern PlatformIO writes to .pio/; .pioenvs/ and .piolibdeps/ are the
# older (pre-modern-PlatformIO) equivalents, kept here defensively in case
# any local toolchain still produces them.
.pio/
.pioenvs/
.piolibdeps/
*.bin
*.elf
*.hex
*.map

# ---- Bench server runtime data (server/server.py) ----------------------------
# covio.db is generated at first run (init_db()) and holds per-installation
# device/telemetry data -- never a source artifact. server/firmware/ is
# where OTA .bin payloads + manifest.json get dropped for local testing
# (server.py's own module docstring); both are runtime-generated, not source.
server/covio.db
server/covio.db-journal

# ---- Native C++ test harness build outputs (test/native_cpp/) ---------------
# RISK-04/RISK-15 phase-2 remediation: local compiler output (this repo has
# no dedicated build directory for these, unlike PlatformIO's .pio/ above),
# never source.
test/native_cpp/*.exe
test/native_cpp/*.pdb
test/native_cpp/*.o
test/native_cpp/*.log

# ---- RISK-16 remediation: OTA manifest signing key -------------------------
# NEVER committed, test or otherwise -- server/tools/sign_manifest.py
# --gen-test-key writes it here for local/CI use only.
server/tools/.test_signing_key.pem

# NOTE on the *.bin rule above: it is intentionally overridden for specific,
# deliberately-committed firmware evidence artifacts (built-and-hashed test
# binaries referenced by the phase-2 audit docs) via `git add -f` at commit
# time, not by a blanket !-negation pattern here -- keeps the default
# "don't track binaries" posture intact everywhere else in the tree.
server/covio.db-wal
server/covio.db-shm
server/firmware/*.bin
server/firmware/manifest.json

# ---- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# ---- Node / Electron -----------------------------------------------------
# Matches anywhere in the tree (no leading slash), not just
# tools/device-manager/ -- defensive coverage for any future JS package.
node_modules/
dist/
npm-debug.log*

# ---- IDE / editor --------------------------------------------------------
# RE-8 audit fix: .vscode/extensions.json is explicitly un-ignored (same
# intent as !.env.example below) -- a shared, checked-in recommended-
# extensions list is exactly the kind of file that SHOULD be tracked, per
# SETUP.md's own "VS Code extensions" section. Every other .vscode/ file
# (settings.json, launch.json, etc.) remains per-developer/local, untracked.
# NOTE: excludes .vscode/*'s CONTENTS (not the directory itself via a
# trailing-slash `.vscode/` pattern) specifically so Git still traverses
# into the directory to evaluate the negation below -- a bare `.vscode/`
# would prune the whole directory first, silently making
# `!.vscode/extensions.json` have no effect at all (a real, easy-to-miss
# .gitignore gotcha: a negation can never re-include a file whose parent
# directory was itself excluded, only a file excluded via the directory's
# *contents* pattern).
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.vs/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# ---- OS artifacts --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---- Logs / scratch -------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp

# ---- Secrets / credential material -------------------------------------
# Audit fix (RE-1 independent audit): defense-in-depth, not a response to an
# active leak -- no such file currently exists in this repository. Directly
# ties to ADR-005's own already-frozen requirement that signing/CA key
# material is "generated and held by Covio and never distributed to the
# field or committed to source control" (Docs/Firmware Detailed
# Architecture Decision Record (ADR).md), and to ordinary CI-secret hygiene
# once RE-4 (GitHub Actions) exists. .env.example (if one is ever added) is
# explicitly un-ignored, since a documented-safe template is exactly the
# opposite of a secret.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
